:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111460","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111460.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111460.patch","merged_at":"2025-10-13T17:37:06Z"},"body":"Follow-up to #111116\r\n\r\nThis adds shortcuts to FileDialogs context menu and buttons.\r\n<img width=\"270\" height=\"121\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6373e207-45f5-424a-9aaf-c4a6a4170fc9\" />\r\n\r\nInterestingly, FileDialog had some shortcuts in action map, but they were never used and instead the dialog was using hard-coded keys. I added missing input actions (including the newly added delete) and changed the shortcut input to use them instead of hard-coded keys.\r\n\r\nNote that once FileDialogs get merged (#111212), some EditorFileDialog shortcuts will be gone:\r\n- Go Back\r\n- Go Forward\r\n- Toggle Favorite\r\n- Toggle Mode\r\n- Move Favorite Up/Down\r\n\r\nI did not add them as input actions, as some of them feel excessive. They can always be re-added later.\r\n\r\nbtw it turns out that PopupMenu supports InputEventAction, so the weird accelerator code in TextEdit could be changed to work like the new FileDialog shortcuts.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/even